#
# ---- verdicts (area 02, 2026-09-28; winoracle = WARP, FL 11_0 device) ----
# Output above is the x64 build. The x86 build is identical except:
#   A BW 1GiB+16 SRV  hr=0x8007000e   (32-bit WARP runs out of address space)
#   A BW 2GiB SRV     hr=0x8007000e
# i.e. an over-large buffer is E_OUTOFMEMORY, never E_INVALIDARG.
#
# Vitreo must be run with a skip list, because these cases ABORT THE HOST
# PROCESS (Metal texture-descriptor validation, SIGABRT) instead of returning
# E_INVALIDARG:
#   B W=16385 R8, B Array=2049, B Mips=8 W=64 (too many), B Mips=16 W=64,
#   C Mips=7 32x16 (too many), C Mips=2 1x1, C Mips=16 16384x1 R8,
#   C Mips=5 4x4 (too many), C S=4 BC1 SRV
# and "GetDesc1" (every ID3D11Texture2D1/3D1::GetDesc1 call jumps to a NULL
# vtable slot: the texture vtable has 11 slots, GetDesc1 is slot 11).
#   ./build/src/vitreo run a02c64.exe -- "B W=16385 R8,B Array=2049,..."
#
# WRONG / MISSING / FATAL against the lines above (Vitreo build 2026-09-27):
#   A CB 65552 / 1048576 / DYN / IMM      Windows S_OK, Vitreo IA (11.1 runtime
#                                        allows CBs > 4096 constants)
#   A ST stride=2052 / 4096               Windows IA, Vitreo OK (max 2048)
#   A RAW BW6 / BW2                       Windows OK, Vitreo IA
#   A DI BW1 / BW4 / BW8                  Windows IA, Vitreo OK (min 12 bytes)
#   A SO|UAV, SO|VB|UAV                   Windows IA, Vitreo OK
#   A RT buffer, RT|SRV buffer            Windows OK, Vitreo IA
#   A BW 1GiB+16 / 2GiB / 0xFFFFFFF0      Windows OK or E_OUTOFMEMORY, Vitreo IA
#   B (Texture1D)                         no validation: every invalid case
#                                        returns S_OK (or S_FALSE with a NULL
#                                        out pointer); W>16384, Array>2048 and
#                                        too many mips abort the host;
#                                        unknown formats return E_NOTIMPL;
#                                        pSysMem NULL is silently skipped;
#                                        initial data fails (E_FAIL) for any
#                                        STAGING 1D texture and, on x64, for
#                                        any 1D texture with >1 subresource
#   C Mips > full chain                   host abort (Windows IA)
#   C S=4 BC1                             host abort (Windows IA)
#   C S=* Q=STANDARD/CENTER               Windows OK, Vitreo IA
#   C CUBE STG                            Windows OK, Vitreo IA
#   C BC top level not multiple of 4      Windows IA, Vitreo OK
#   C BC RT / UAV                         Windows IA, Vitreo OK
#   C BC DYN                              Windows OK, Vitreo IA
#   C GDI_COMPATIBLE (all legal shapes)   Windows OK, Vitreo IA
#   C DYN mips>1 / array>1                Windows IA, Vitreo OK
#   C depth DS|UAV                        Windows IA, Vitreo OK
#   C R24G8 SRV/bind0, R24_UNORM_X8 SRV,
#     D32 bind0                           Windows OK, Vitreo IA
#   C R24_UNORM_X8 DS, SH|NT D24S8 DS     Windows IA, Vitreo OK
#   C R8G8_B8G8 4x2, D R32G32B32_FLOAT    Windows OK, Vitreo IA (formats)
#   D bind0 DEF, IMM CL, GM RT|SRV|UAV    Windows OK, Vitreo IA
#   D BC1 5x5x1                           Windows IA, Vitreo OK
#   E T1D invalid + NULL out              Windows IA, Vitreo S_FALSE
#   F BUF non-structured stride           Windows GetDesc S=0, Vitreo echoes 16
#   F GDI / RESOURCE_CLAMP                (creation refused, see C)
#   G default eviction priority           Windows 0x78000000 (NORMAL), Vitreo 0
#   G buffer / tex3d QI(IDXGIResource)    Windows S_OK, Vitreo E_NOINTERFACE
#   G tex1d QI                            Windows answers ID3D11Texture1D only;
#                                        Vitreo answers ID3D11Texture2D and
#                                        refuses ID3D11Texture1D
#   H T2D pitch8 (<row)                   Windows OK (reads at the given
#                                        pitch), Vitreo IA
#   H T2D/T3D last row/slice at page end Windows OK, Vitreo IA: Vitreo reads
